-- title:
--   Complex uniformisation of the quaternionic moduli curve with correspondences
-- statement:
--   Fix naturals $N$ (nonzero, squarefree) and primes $q \neq q'$ neither dividing $N$, and a natural $D$ divisible by $2Nqq'$. Let $a,b \in \mathbb{Q}$ be such that $B = \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ satisfies `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt`: $0 < a$ or $0 < b$, and for a finite place $v$ of $\mathbb{Q}$ every nonzero element of $B \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_v$ is a unit exactly when $v$ lies above $q$ or $q'$. Let $\Lambda$ be a maximal order, $R \leq \Lambda$ an Eichler order of level $N$ (an intersection of two maximal orders with relative index $N$ in one of them), and $\iota : B \to M_2(\mathbb{R})$ an injective $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra map. Let $X$ be an integral scheme with a smooth proper morphism $\pi_X$ of relative dimension $1$ to $\operatorname{Spec} \mathbb{Z}[1/D]$, having integral geometric fibres, together with a map $\mathrm{pt}$ sending a fake elliptic curve over $S$ with $\Lambda$-action and level $N$ to an $X$-point over a given base point, assumed invariant under isomorphism, compatible with pullback along ring maps, and bijective on isomorphism classes over algebraically closed fields. Let $\bar{s}$ be a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point of the base compatible with $\mathbb{Z} \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, let $\bar{F}$ be a one-variable function field over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (essentially of finite type, with principal divisors, finite residue extensions and $\Omega_{\bar F/\overline{\mathbb{Q}}}$ free of rank one) carrying a Galois action $\mathrm{gal}$ by semilinear automorphisms and a curve model $\mathfrak{M}$ whose underlying scheme is identified by an isomorphism $e_{\mathfrak{M}}$ with the fibre of $\pi_X$ over $\bar{s}$, compatibly with the structure maps. Let $\mathbb{T}$ be tower data over $\bar F$ for the primes away from $q,q'$ (fields $\mathbb{T}.F(\ell)$ with two finite integral $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-embeddings of $\bar F$ each), with Galois actions $\mathrm{galT}$, semilinear involutions $W : \mathrm{Fin}\,2 \to \mathrm{SemilinearAut}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}, \bar F)$ and $WT$, and let $tw$ be a witness of `ModuliTowerWitnessD` for all of these data. Then there exist a field $F_c$ that is a one-variable function field over $\mathbb{C}$ (essentially of finite type), a `UniformizedHeckeCurve` structure $U$ on $F_c$ for the Fuchsian group $\mathrm{fuchsianGroup}\ R\ \iota$ (the image under $\iota$ of the group generated by the units of $R$, intersected with the kernel of the determinant), a ring embedding $\mathrm{emb} : \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to \mathbb{C}$, a ring map $\mathrm{toC} : \bar F \to F_c$ and a map $\mathrm{bcPlace}$ on places, such that: $U.\mathrm{pt} : \mathbb{H} \to \mathrm{Place}\ \mathbb{C}\ F_c$ is surjective; for every prime $\ell$ there is a finite set $S \subseteq B$ of elements of $R$ of reduced norm $\ell$, each represented by an element of $\mathrm{levelHeckeUSet}\ \Lambda\ R\ \ell$ if $\ell \mid N$ and of $\mathrm{primeHeckeSet}\ R\ \ell$ otherwise, such that every $y \in R$ of reduced norm $\ell$ so represented is $u x$ for a unique $x \in S$ and some unit $u$ of $R$ of reduced norm $1$, and the multiset $U.\mathrm{heckePoints}\ \ell$, viewed in $M_2(\mathbb{R})$, is the image of $S$ under $\iota$; $U.\mathrm{realize}$ sends each element of $F_c$ to a function on the upper half plane meromorphic at every point, is additive, multiplicative, sends scalars to constants, is injective up to germs off each point, is invariant under the Fuchsian group, and hits every meromorphic Fuchsian-invariant function; $\mathrm{toC}$ is compatible with $\mathrm{emb}$ on $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, the subfield of $F_c$ generated by $\mathbb{C}$ and $\mathrm{toC}(\bar F)$ is everything, $\mathrm{toC}$ carries $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-linearly independent finite families to $\mathbb{C}$-linearly independent ones, and $\mathrm{bcPlace}$ is compatible with valuation subrings along $\mathrm{toC}$; and finally the correspondences match: for each prime $\ell \neq q, q'$ the operator $U.\mathrm{corr}\ \ell$ agrees, after pushing divisors forward along $\mathrm{bcPlace}$, with the push–pull correspondence $(\mathbb{T}.\varphi(\ell,1))_* (\mathbb{T}.\varphi(\ell,0))^*$ on divisors of $\bar F$, while $U.\mathrm{corr}\ q$ and $U.\mathrm{corr}\ q'$ agree with the maps on divisors induced by the actions of $W\,0$ and $W\,1$ on places.
--
--   This is Shimura's complex uniformisation of the coarse moduli curve of fake elliptic curves with $\Lambda$-action and level-$N$ structure: its geometric function field over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ becomes, after base change along an embedding $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \hookrightarrow \mathbb{C}$, the field of automorphic functions for the Fuchsian group attached to the Eichler order $R$, and the dictionary between places and points of the upper half plane transports the Hecke correspondences at all primes — the push–pull correspondences along the tower away from $q,q'$, and the Atkin–Lehner involutions $W\,0, W\,1$ at $q$ and $q'$. It supplies the analytic comparison data for [`CerednikDrinfeld.exists_shimuraCurveModel_rigidModuliWitness_heckeTower_of_six_mul_dvd_of_neZero`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.exists_shimuraCurveModel_rigidModuliWitness_heckeTower_of_six_mul_dvd_of_neZero).
